{"packet_id":"D010-01","doc_id":"D010","jurisdiction":"Boston, MA","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Boston Fair Chance Tenant Selection Policy — criminal record screening limits","requirement":"A housing provider may not impose a blanket denial based on arrests or convictions; it must review applicants case by case and may not consider non-convictions, sealed or expunged convictions, juvenile records, or convictions older than 5 years.","key_value":"5 years (conviction lookback)","coverage_conditions":"Housing providers receiving DND funding and/or land, or with income-restricted units created under the BPDA Inclusionary Development Policy; also applied to the Office of Fair Housing and Equity Affirmative Marketing Program.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Housing providers receiving DND funding or land, or with BPDA Inclusionary Development Policy income-restricted units"},"exemptions":"Arrest and conviction screening limits do not apply where there is a direct relationship between the conviction and the housing sought or an unreasonable risk of substantial harm to others, or to current criminal behavior.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2017-02","citation":"Boston Fair Chance Tenant Selection Policy (Feb. 2017), ¶ 1","quoted_span":"a) Arrests that did not result in conviction. This includes dismissed charges, diversion programs, and similar non-convictions.
b) Convictions that are subject to a form of judicial relief, such as expungement, sealing, and certificates for relief from disabilities.
c) Juvenile records
d) A conviction more than 5 years old.","interaction":"Federal or state law imposing a criminal history requirement that conflicts with this policy preempts it.","confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D010-01","doc_id":"D010","jurisdiction":"Boston, MA","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Boston Fair Chance Tenant Selection Policy — credit screening limits","requirement":"A housing provider may not use an applicant's credit score to approve or deny housing; credit history may be used only in place of rental history to judge ability to pay, and lack of credit history alone is not grounds to reject.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Housing providers receiving DND funding and/or land, or with income-restricted units created under the BPDA Inclusionary Development Policy; also applied to the Office of Fair Housing and Equity Affirmative Marketing Program.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Housing providers receiving DND funding or land, or with BPDA Inclusionary Development Policy income-restricted units"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2017-02","citation":"Boston Fair Chance Tenant Selection Policy (Feb. 2017), ¶ 5","quoted_span":"a) The agent agrees not to use the applicant credit score to approve or deny housing applications.

b) Property Managers may consider an applicant’s credit history, but such information may ONLY be used in lieu of rental history to determine an applicant’s ability to pay rent when rental history is not available.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
